sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-echinarachnius-parma-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-echinarachnius-parma-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-echinarachnius-parma-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Echinarachnius parma Holocene 60 µm Schnakenberg Turing wavelength — MorphoEval overall 86.8/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 1 score 86.8. The script integrates Schnakenberg kinetics with a Turing dispersion peak on a periodic 480 µm patch (eight 60 µm wavelengths) at age 0 Ma. The equilibrated FFT wavelength is 60.336 µm (linear peak 61.343 µm). A seven-point diffusivity sweep tracks the linear prediction with Pearson r = 0.9965 and RMSE 2.575 µm. Equal diffusion collapses the activator standard deviation to 5.69e-3, and a 10 µm patch (the predecessor tier) stays at amplitude 0. The USNM E39365 CC0 plate is SHA-256 pinned and shown beside the lattice; the growth GIF is 560 px and 12 frames (computer-vision similarity 85.2 against that plate). The union mask treats three tests as one object, the KS statistic is computed on only seven wavelengths, and the quenched bar is invisible on a linear axis. Overall 86.8/100 (faithfulness 86.0, reproducibility 88.8); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 2340b0d2; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 82, Parameter expressivity 88, Morphometric validation 86, Source and data traceability 92, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/echinarachnius_parma_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-echinarachnius-parma-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 2340b0d2, image/png, 417295 B, 1512×984 px, artifact_sha256 ff8643dfdb5d8f2e95dad538bd4f79b2c10eba0af3349d7b80b6fdcfc7ffb9dc (sha256 ff8643dfdb5d8f2e95dad538bd4f79b2c10eba0af3349d7b80b6fdcfc7ffb9dc), spec_fingerprint e8201a3df779a67d8e85472abacbae9a6fbc7d0d99dd6ba261bbc538d065da4c. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: e8201a3df779a67d8e85472abacbae9a6fbc7d0d99dd6ba261bbc538d065da4c; artifact_sha256: ff8643dfdb5d8f2e95dad538bd4f79b2c10eba0af3349d7b80b6fdcfc7ffb9dc; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/echinarachnius_parma_turing_wavelength_s0/echinarachnius_parma_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=35136a28b3d11ab4..., datasets/echinarachnius_parma_turing_wavelength_s0/echinarachnius_parma_usnm_e39365_specimen.jpeg=1af65dc69de55d4b...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing (1952) diffusion-driven instability at a finite wavenumber when the inhibitor diffuses faster than the activator | Schnakenberg (1979) kinetics a - u + u^2 v and b - u^2 v, published for limit cycles and used here as the standard two-species Turing extension | Gierer and Meinhardt (1972) short-range activation with long-range inhibition; Kondo and Miura (2010) review of reaction-diffusion as a patterning framework | Seilacher (1979) constructional morphology of the sand-dollar test at centimetre scale (petaloids, dome, pressure drainage); reconstructed_in_script: Periodic Fourier IMEX integration of the Schnakenberg system on a 480 µm patch, Du = 28.006 µm²/time, Dv = 336.069 µm²/time (ratio 12), seed 3214 | Linear dispersion peak λ = 61.343 µm and equilibrated FFT wavelength λ = 60.336 µm | Diffusivity-scale sweep with Pearson r = 0.9965, RMSE = 2.575 µm; equal-diffusion ablation amplitude 5.69e-3; 10 µm patch amplitude 0 | Union-mask segmentation of the CC0 USNM E39365 plate (foreground fraction 0.357, union circularity 0.066, coherency 0.404); transfer_boundary: Du and Dv are chosen so the equilibrated lattice sits on the assigned 60 µm detail scale. They are not measured diffusion coefficients of sand-dollar epithelium. | The 60 µm wavelength is the slot scale. Seilacher (1979) does not report it. | The chronoseries has one member (Holocene, 0 Ma). The predecessor and successor contrasted here are scale tiers (10 µm and 600 µm), not older named species. | The rendered disc is a 480 µm patch coloured with the plate's mean pigment. It is not a photograph of a whole test, and the union mask does not separate the three individuals.; does_not_claim: A measured echinochrome diffusion constant, a gene-regulatory network for E. parma pigment, or a fit to the centimetre-scale petaloid | That sibling slot 160's dimensionless parameters (α = 1.71, β = 0.43) apply at 60 µm." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Mark the quenched 10 µm amplitude on the comparison figure so a zero bar is readable.",
            "remediation needed: Replace the 7-point wavelength KS (D moves in steps of 1/7) with a Kolmogorov-Smirnov comparison of the ocellus nearest-neighbour sample against the FFT wavelength, and record the spacing coefficient of variation.",
            "remediation needed: Split USNM E39365 into connected components and report per-disc circularity and aspect ratio. The union circularity 0.066 describes three tests on a black ground, not an individual sand dollar." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.868"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (primary assessor, Pass 1)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://x.ai> .
}

